# Add a talon (+ GraphQL)

Use for **new** behavior. To **replace** a core Peregrine talon, mirror it under `src/overrides/peregrine/...` (override resolver) instead.

1. Create `src/talons/<Feature>/use<Feature>.js` — the hook.
2. Co-locate GraphQL in `src/talons/<Feature>/<feature>.gql.js`.
3. Wire UI from `src/components/<Feature>/` (one component per file; split sub-components).
4. Import via aliases — `@/talons/...`, `@/components/...`.
5. User-facing strings the talon returns should be `{ id, defaultMessage }` shaped (rendered with `formatMessage`), especially validator messages.

| Situation | Approach |
|---|---|
| New hook/logic, no core file replaced | talon in `src/talons/` (this) |
| Replace a core Peregrine talon | override resolver (`src/overrides/peregrine/`) |
| Replace a whole module export | targetable splice |
